a)  
\[
D=E+\lambda \overrightarrow{EF}=(0,1,3)+\lambda(3,1,0)=(3\lambda,1+\lambda,3)
\]

\[
V_T(\lambda)=\frac{1}{6}\left|
\begin{matrix}
2 & 0 & 1/2\\
3/2 & 3 & 1\\
3\lambda & 1+\lambda & 3
\end{matrix}
\right|
=\frac{1}{6}\left(-\frac{9\lambda}{2}-\frac{5}{4}(1+\lambda)+18\right)
\]

\[
V_T(\lambda)=\frac{67-23\lambda}{24}
\]

Como \(\lambda\in[0,1]\), el volumen máximo se alcanza en \(\lambda=0\):

\[
V_{\max}=V_T(0)=\frac{67}{24}\simeq 2.7917\ \text{m}^3
\]

---

b)  
Si \(\lambda=1\),

\[
V_T(1)=\frac{67-23}{24}=\frac{44}{24}=\frac{11}{6}
\]

\[
V_T(1)=\frac{1}{3}S_{ABC}\cdot H
\]

\[
H=\frac{3V_T(1)}{S_{ABC}}
\]

Calculamos el área de la base:

\[
S_{ABC}=\frac{1}{2}\left\|\overrightarrow{AB}\times \overrightarrow{AC}\right\|
\]

\[
S_{ABC}=\frac{1}{2}\left|
\begin{matrix}
\vec i & \vec j & \vec k\\
2 & 0 & 1/2\\
3/2 & 3 & 1
\end{matrix}
\right|
=\frac{1}{2}\left\|\left(-\frac{3}{2},\frac{5}{4},6\right)\right\|
\]

\[
S_{ABC}=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\frac{9}{4}+\frac{25}{16}+36}
=\frac{1}{8}\sqrt{637}
=\frac{7\sqrt{13}}{8}\ \text{m}^2
\]

Por tanto,

\[
H=\frac{3\cdot \frac{11}{6}}{\frac{7\sqrt{13}}{8}}
=\frac{44\sqrt{13}}{91}
\]

\[
H\simeq 1.7433\ \text{m}
\]","A continuacion tienes el texto completo del documento de enunciados.

